comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-18T23:18:44.432Z","harness:codex","Live lineage verification: closed pm-xm0id4 already changed default CLI/MCP closure to retain predecessor rows. This issue is completed at the public SDK explicit orderingEdges=remove boundary: remove and report use one selected row set, emit every removed predecessor plus a row count, and distinguish the transient blocked_by scalar. The original implementation failed the three-predecessor regression; existing preserved-edge behavior remains covered. Focused cross-component regression suite passed 365 tests."
  "2026-09-18T23:35:58.930Z","harness:codex","Both linked test groups pass. Installed npm and Bun SDK consumers each closed a real three-predecessor item with explicit removal, observed all three IDs and count=3, and verified the persisted item no longer contained those dependencies. The default preserve path remains covered in the existing CLI close suite."
  "2026-09-19T00:13:37.815Z","harness:codex","Final source verification: all 9039 tests in 714 files pass. Exact coverage is statements 64887/64887, branches 49530/49530, functions 13467/13467 and lines 62103/62103. Module, exported-declaration and member documentation coverage is 100 percent. Typechecks, ESLint, duplicate detection, docs/skills, installed npm/Bun and packed npx/bunx acceptance pass; production and development dependency audit and credential scanning report no findings. The final neutral test environment removes ambient session IDs while preserving harness identity and normal probe behavior. Prior temporary quota and environment failures remain documented separately."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-18T23:29:09.346Z","harness:codex","A lifecycle warning must describe the exact rows selected for mutation. Count dependency rows separately from transient blocked-state scalars, and retain duplicate targets when their rows carry distinct provenance. Default terminal closure preserves historical predecessor facts."
